From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:42:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [zlib][x86] Check CPU and OS support before AVX-512
 CRC-32

With CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL (CMake ENABLE_SIMD_AVX512), the AVX-512
CRC-32 kernel is enabled by _xgetbv(0) & 0x40 alone:

- XGETBV faults unless the CPU has XSAVE and the OS enabled OSXSAVE.
- CPUID is never checked for AVX-512F or VPCLMULQDQ, so AVX-512 CPUs
  without VPCLMULQDQ (e.g. Skylake-X) fault in the kernel.
- XCR0 bit 6 alone does not mean the XMM, YMM and opmask state is
  enabled.

Check XSAVE/OSXSAVE before XGETBV and the maximum CPUID leaf before
leaf 7, then AVX-512F, VPCLMULQDQ and XCR0 0xe6, plus the SSE2, PCLMULQDQ,
SSE4.1 and AVX bits the kernel itself uses, instead of relying on
x86_cpu_enable_simd to imply them.

Also zero the upper lanes of the initial CRC vector. Those of
_mm512_castsi128_si512 are undefined: an unoptimized clang build
computed wrong CRCs whenever the registers held stale data. Use
_mm512_inserti32x4 with zero rather than _mm512_zextsi128_si512, which
GCC before 10 lacks.

GN builds do not define CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL and are unchanged.
Tested on AMD Zen 4 (AVX-512 with VPCLMULQDQ).

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
